2026-04-09 Update - Spec 004 Free-Flow Guardrail:
- Revisited spec `004-private-accounts` to protect the core free product behavior.
- Added a new constitution rule in `.specify/memory/constitution.md` stating that the unauthenticated self-entry flow is a core product invariant.
- Documented that:
- a manager must still be able to invite an organization by email and have people add themselves without login
- unreserved email addresses must remain addable through the public flow
- non-owned organizations must keep the public self-entry path
- account/admin/privacy features must layer on top of that free flow instead of replacing it
- Updated `specs/004-private-accounts/spec.md` to make the free self-entry model explicit in scope boundaries, product rules, requirements, and success criteria.
- Updated `specs/004-private-accounts/plan.md` so the free flow is treated as a permanent product mode and included in verification strategy.
- Updated `specs/004-private-accounts/tasks.md` to add:
- `T0415` for the explicit non-regression rule
- `T0436` for regression coverage proving the public unreserved-email flow still works without login
- Current impact assessment:
- no implementation work from spec `004` has landed yet
- the main risk was ambiguous spec wording, not shipped code
- no known current behavior regression was introduced by spec `004` implementation because spec `004` implementation has not started

2026-04-09 Update - Spec 004 Phase 2 Decisions:
- Completed the phase-2 design block for `specs/004-private-accounts/`.
- Authentication/session decision (`T0410`):
- selected server-side browser session auth using `HttpSession`/`JSESSIONID` for private-account features
- explicitly rejected JWT for v1 because the app is already server-rendered and the simpler session model keeps the public flow untouched
- Persistence decision (`T0411`):
- keep `Person` as the org-chart row model so the free self-entry path remains intact
- define organizations as `OPEN` versus `OFFICIAL`
- add explicit new models for `Account`, `EmailVerificationCode`, `OrganizationMembership`, and `DomainVerificationChallenge`
- model org-specific admin and approval state on membership rather than on the user account
- Abuse-control decision (`T0412`):
- verification codes are single-use
- a new send invalidates older pending codes for that account/email
- code lifetime is 15 minutes
- resend lockout is 5 minutes
- daily cap is 5 sends in the trailing 24 hours
- Domain/admin safety decision (`T0413`):
- v1 claim flow can convert an existing `OPEN` org into an `OFFICIAL` org
- v1 does not allow DNS takeover of an already `OFFICIAL` org
- `OFFICIAL` orgs may never be left with zero approved admins
- Private-chart authorization decision (`T0414`):
- private org charts are visible only to approved members of that organization
- provisional members, rejected members, outsiders, and unauthenticated visitors cannot view private charts
- Free-flow non-regression decision (`T0415`):
- unreserved emails remain addable without login in `OPEN` organizations
- `OFFICIAL` controls must not spill into `OPEN` orgs
- added a regression-testing task to enforce that no-login public self-entry still works for the free path
- Updated files:
- `.specify/memory/constitution.md`
- `specs/004-private-accounts/spec.md`
- `specs/004-private-accounts/plan.md`
