2026-04-09 Update - Spec 004 Phase 3 Implementation:
- Implemented the account-and-verification foundation for `004-private-accounts` without changing the public person/org flow.
- Added account domain objects under `src/main/java/com/fishdan/myorgchart/account/`:
- `Account`
- `EmailVerificationCode`
- `EmailVerificationCodeStatus`
- `AccountRepository`
- `EmailVerificationCodeRepository`
- `AccountService`
- `AccountController`
- `AccountSession`
- `VerificationCodeGenerator`
- `NumericVerificationCodeGenerator`
- `VerificationEmailSender`
- `AwsSesVerificationEmailSender`
- Reused the existing `PasswordEncoder` bean for both account passwords and hashed verification-code storage so plaintext credentials/codes are not persisted.
- Added a `Clock` bean and an AWS SES v2 client bean in `src/main/java/com/fishdan/myorgchart/MyOrgChartApplication.java`.
- Added server-rendered account pages:
- `src/main/resources/templates/register.html`
- `src/main/resources/templates/login.html`
- `src/main/resources/templates/verify-account.html`
- Updated `src/main/java/com/fishdan/myorgchart/PageController.java` and `src/main/resources/templates/index.html` to expose the private-account entry points while keeping the free no-login instructions and main actions intact.
- Added repo-safe SES configuration in `src/main/resources/application.properties`:
- `APP_EMAIL_FROM_ADDRESS`
- optional `APP_EMAIL_CONFIGURATION_SET`
- SES integration detail:
- verification emails are sent through AWS SES v2 using a verified sender identity and optional configuration set, matching the SES-oriented infrastructure pattern documented in `../fishdan-terraform/aws/ses.tf`
- Verification-code behavior implemented:
- single-use codes
- 15-minute expiry
- new send invalidates older pending codes
- resend blocked for 5 minutes
- capped at 5 sends per trailing 24 hours
- Login/session behavior implemented:
- browser flows use server-side session state via `HttpSession`
- verified users redirect to home after login
- unverified users redirect to the verify-account flow
- Free-flow guardrail validation:
- no changes were made to `PersonController`, `PersonService`, or the public create-person/create-organization/public-org-chart flow semantics for unreserved emails
- Added automated coverage:
- `src/test/java/com/fishdan/myorgchart/account/AccountServiceTest.java`
- `src/test/java/com/fishdan/myorgchart/account/AccountControllerTest.java`
