2026-04-02 Update - Mockito Test Harness Hardening:
- During full-suite validation on Java 21, Maven test output showed Mockito self-attaching a Byte Buddy agent at runtime and the JVM warned that dynamic agent loading will be disallowed by default in a future JDK.
- Confirmed the repo does not contain a custom Mockito extension file under `src/test/resources`, so the behavior came from the default Mockito/Spring test stack rather than a repo-local override.
- Resolved the warning by configuring `maven-surefire-plugin` in `pom.xml` to launch tests with an explicit Mockito Java agent:
- `-javaagent:${settings.localRepository}/org/mockito/mockito-core/${mockito.version}/mockito-core-${mockito.version}.jar`
- Validation after the fix:
- `mvn test -q`
- `SPRING_DATASOURCE_URL='jdbc:mariadb://fishdanaws.cvkyaweq6ujr.us-east-1.rds.amazonaws.com:3306/myorgchart' SPRING_DATASOURCE_USERNAME='dbmaster' SPRING_DATASOURCE_PASSWORD='***' npm run test:e2e`
- Result:
- backend tests passed
- Playwright E2E suite passed with `7 passed`
- The prior Mockito self-attach warning no longer appears. One unrelated JVM CDS warning remains:
- `Sharing is only supported for boot loader classes because bootstrap classpath has been appended`

