2026-04-09 Update - Spec 004 Phase 5 Official Domains And Claims:
- Added organization ownership state so organizations are now explicitly `OPEN` or `OFFICIAL`.
- Added domain-verification challenge persistence with generated TXT challenge tokens in the form `fdorgchart-verification=...`.
- Added a DNS TXT lookup abstraction with:
- JNDI-based TXT lookup for non-dev runtimes
- dev-only in-memory TXT storage and endpoints so the flow can be validated locally without touching real DNS
- Added a settings-page flow to:
- start a domain verification challenge
- display the TXT value to publish
- re-check the TXT record
- show the organizations the current account now administers
- Implemented verification rules:
- only verified accounts can manage official-domain claims
- verification checks are capped at once every 10 minutes per challenge
- existing `OPEN` organizations can be claimed
- already-`OFFICIAL` organizations reject re-claim attempts in v1
- On successful verification:
- the organization is marked `OFFICIAL`
- a new organization is created automatically when the verified domain does not yet exist
- the verifying account becomes the first recorded admin for that organization
- Added test-cleanup support for domain challenges, admin rows, and dev TXT records so browser runs remain isolated.
- Validation:
- `bash ./mvnw -q test`
- `SPRING_DATASOURCE_USERNAME=root SPRING_DATASOURCE_PASSWORD=mysql npm run test:e2e`
- Result:
- backend tests passed
- Playwright passed with `11 passed`
- Scope note:
- this phase establishes official-domain ownership and first-admin assignment only
- provisional-member approvals and admin delegation remain intentionally deferred to phase 6
- Speckit completion note:
- `T0440` through `T0445` are complete

2026-04-09 Update - Spec 004 Phase 6 Admin Controls And Provisional Members:
- Added explicit membership approval state on `Person` rows:
- `APPROVED`
- `PROVISIONAL`
- `REJECTED`
- Preserved the free-flow behavior for `OPEN` organizations:
- public and authenticated self-entry remain immediately approved there
- official-domain controls do not spill back into open organizations
- Added official-domain membership behavior:
- public create-person submissions to `OFFICIAL` organizations are rejected
- verified self-adds to `OFFICIAL` organizations become provisional unless the joining account is already an org admin
- provisional members are excluded from the org-chart API for official organizations
- Added admin review and role-management support in the settings page:
- approve provisional member
- reject provisional member
- grant admin to an approved member with a verified private account
- revoke admin from an approved member
- Added last-admin safety enforcement:
- official organizations cannot be left with zero admins
- admin revocation now rejects the final remaining admin
- Added test coverage for:
- public add rejection against official organizations
- org-chart filtering of provisional members
- admin permission checks and last-admin safety
- browser flow covering official-org self-join, provisional hidden state, approval, and admin promotion
